		"title": "The Offering of Garrow",
		"story": "That was the year the storm came down on the Carrow house. When the air cleared, the family was gone, and in their place stood people in furs who spoke like the old songs - the Carrows' own forebears. The forebears read the strange world as their gods' anger. At dusk they took Garrow to the stake, and the drums began. At dawn Kell made the offering, as their fathers had."
